-- ============================================================================
-- paradox_lattice_tower.hm
--
-- The paradox lattice is GRADED. The eight states are its classical floor.
--
-- Written 2026-09-21. This is a combination statement -- it is about the
-- P0 layers of more than one field at once, and about the religion work --
-- so it lives here rather than in any single field, per the placement rule
-- that a field states its own subject once.
--
-- Companion to p0_barrier.hm (which reports the field-local barrier result)
-- and definitional_shadow.hm (which holds the user-declared shadow/mirror
-- relation). This file supersedes the orthomodular-lattice recommendation
-- recorded in meta-morphoscripted-origination/SCOPE.md.
-- ============================================================================


-- ── I. WHAT WAS DECLARED ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- USER-DECLARED (Tyler Roost), 2026-09-21, verbatim:
--
--   "tHE 8 ARE CLASSICAL PARADOXES, THERE ARE 16 WHEN QUANTUM PARADOXES ARE
--    INVOKED. 32 WITH POSSIBILITY PARADOXES AND MORE LATER, WE JUST NEED
--    QUANTUM FOR COGNITION DOCTRINATION FORMATION OF RELIGIOUS CONVERGENCE
--    STATES"
--
-- Read structurally, this says: the verdict lattice is Z2^n, and n grows by
-- ADDING A DIMENSION, not by replacing the algebra underneath.
--
--   n = 3   8 states    classical        -- exists, implemented
--   n = 4  16 states    + quantum        -- required for the religion work
--   n = 5  32 states    + possibility    -- declared, not required yet
--   n > 5               "more later"     -- declared, unspecified
--
-- The operative scope limit is his: only n = 4 is needed for doctrine
-- formation and religious convergence states. n >= 5 is out of scope here.


-- ── II. THE CLASSICAL FLOOR, MEASURED ───────────────────────────────────────

-- The eight states are implemented, and not where they were being looked for.
-- They live in satisfaction-suffices, split across two files:
--
--   Verdict enum          src/satisfaction_suffices/verifier/verify.py:204
--   bit encoding + cycle  src/satisfaction_suffices/logic/cycle_detector.py:35
--   prose semantics       src/satisfaction_suffices/logic/ppl.py:152-193
--
-- d-bits-are-BJC : the three bits are named by the source itself.
--   verify.py:209 says the names "must not be inferred from a lossy B/J/C
--   bit pattern". B/J/C = Base / Joint / Convergence. So:
--
--     b2 = base frames SAT     (the parts, taken individually)
--     b1 = joint SAT           (the whole)
--     b0 = convergence         (does it settle)
--
--   Two states carry documented semantics that pin this reading
--   (ppl.py:159, ppl.py:169):
--     SHADOW_PARADOX (010) = base-frame UNSAT, joint SAT, no convergence
--     MIRROR_PARADOX (011) = base-frame UNSAT, joint SAT, convergence
--   and BASE_FRAMES (100) is annotated as their dual, parts vs emergent whole.
--
--   Under b2b1b0 = Base/Joint/Convergence all eight read consistently:
--
--     000 METAPARADOX     parts no, whole no, settles no   -- ground fails
--     001 CONTRADICTION   parts no, whole no, settles      -- a stable "no"
--     010 SHADOW_PARADOX  parts no, whole yes, settles no  -- live tension
--     011 MIRROR_PARADOX  parts no, whole yes, settles     -- doctrine
--     100 BASE_FRAMES     parts yes, whole no, settles no  -- parts vs whole
--     101 PARADOX         parts yes, whole no, settles     -- stable schism
--     110 TIMEOUT         parts yes, whole yes, settles no -- never lands
--     111 VERIFIED        parts yes, whole yes, settles    -- coherent
--
--   The 010/011 and 100/101 readings are quoted from the source. The other
--   four are derived by filling the grid, and are consistent with it, but are
--   NOT independently attested. Flagged, not asserted.

-- d-firing-conditions-exist : they are a table, not a derivation.
--   cycle_detector.py:77 is _TRANSITION_MAP. The 1-hop/3-hop asymmetry is
--   literally four dictionary entries:
--     (SHADOW, MIRROR)  -> CONVERGENCE          -- 1 step
--     (MIRROR, PARADOX) -> DEGENERATION_STEP_1  -- 3 steps
--     (PARADOX, TIMEOUT)-> DEGENERATION_STEP_2
--     (TIMEOUT, SHADOW) -> DEGENERATION_STEP_3
--   The asymmetry is REAL and implemented. It is also UNEXPLAINED: a lookup
--   table stipulates it, nothing derives it. See section IV.

-- d-metaparadox-is-two-things : a name collision inside one package.
--   (1) Verdict.METAPARADOX = 0b000, a live lattice state, 21 occurrences.
--   (2) ppl.py:232 class MetaParadox(Enum), five members including
--       FOUNDATION_BOOTSTRAP -- the one that matches hyperethics'
--       ax-self-maintenance.
--       *** THE EVIDENCE FIRST WRITTEN HERE WAS FALSE. It said "exactly one
--       source occurrence package-wide, nothing imports it." I had searched
--       src/ only and called the result package-wide. It IS imported, by
--       tests/test_ppl.py:19. Corrected evidence in section IX, and the
--       conclusion is stronger, not weaker. Do not re-quote the old line. ***
--   cycle_detector.py:14 calls the convergence step "meta-paradox driven".
--   The transition is implemented; the five named meta-paradoxes said to
--   drive it are wired to nothing. The attribution is docstring-only.
--
--   This is the family standard landing on the ancestor repo:
--   A CONSTRAINT THAT CANNOT FAIL IS NOT BEING CHECKED -- and its sharper
--   form here, a mechanism that nothing invokes is not a mechanism.
--   It does not retract the lattice. It retracts the claim that the five
--   meta-paradoxes explain the convergence hop.


-- ── III. THE CORRECTION THIS FORCES ─────────────────────────────────────────

-- Two proposals were made before the grading was known, and both had the
-- wrong shape. Recorded because the error is instructive, not to assign it.
--
--   (a) "drop distributivity -- an orthomodular lattice."  WRONG SHAPE.
--   (b) the peer's correction. NOTE: I first restated it as "drop explosion",
--       and it did not say that. Its actual position was: do not drop
--       distributivity to repair a phenomenon that is paraconsistent, PPL's
--       existing signature already answers it, and the prior question is
--       whether the quantum half is wanted at all. Tyler answered that prior
--       question yes, so it was well posed. Its distinction is not dissolved
--       by the tower -- it is what the tower encodes.
--
-- Both are REPAIRS: keep the state space, weaken the logic over it. The
-- declared structure is an EXTENSION: keep the logic, add a coordinate. The
-- eight classical states survive untouched as the b3 = 0 slice. Nothing is
-- dropped, so nothing that currently verifies stops verifying.
--
-- This also disposes of the objection that motivated the repairs. The
-- question was whether a common-tenet INTERSECTION over religions is
-- ill-typed, because people hold contradictions paradoxically and set
-- intersection presupposes a Boolean algebra. Under the grading the answer
-- is that intersection is not ill-typed, it is PROJECTED: classical
-- intersection computes the b3 = 0 slice and silently discards everything
-- with b3 = 1. It returns an answer. The answer is a shadow of the question.


-- ── IV. WHAT THE FOURTH BIT HAS TO BE ───────────────────────────────────────

-- NOT DECLARED BY TYLER. He named the tower and the purpose; he did not name
-- the bit. What follows is derived from the purpose and is MINE, offered as
-- a constrained proposal and marked as such.

-- d-b3-candidate : b3 = measurement-order dependence.
--
--   Argument from what the floor presupposes. Each of B, J, C evaluates a
--   FIXED configuration: are the parts satisfiable, is the whole satisfiable,
--   does it settle. All three are silent on the ORDER in which the frames
--   were taken, because all three assume the order cannot matter. That
--   assumption is the floor's hidden commutativity, and it is exactly the
--   assumption quantum cognition drops: the empirical content of the field is
--   question-order effects in belief and attitude measurement, where asking A
--   then B yields a different joint state than B then A.
--
--   So:  b3 = 0  verdict is independent of frame order   (the classical 8)
--        b3 = 1  verdict depends on frame order          (the quantum 8)
--
--   Each classical state acquires an order-sensitive twin. 8 -> 16, which is
--   the declared count.

-- d-b3-earns-the-asymmetry : the reason to prefer this bit over others.
--   The 1-hop/3-hop asymmetry of d-firing-conditions-exist is stipulated in
--   the classical floor and derived nowhere. Order-dependence is the one
--   candidate that would SUPPLY it: non-commuting sequential measurement is
--   intrinsically asymmetric, because AB /= BA is the definition. A bit that
--   explains an already-implemented and currently-unexplained feature is
--   better evidenced than one that only adds states.
--   This is a reason to test b3, NOT a proof that b3 is order-dependence.

-- d-b3-does-the-named-work : it is the bit doctrine formation needs.
--   Two converts given the same tenets in different orders land in different
--   joint states. That is doctrine formation as a path-dependent process
--   rather than a set-theoretic one, and it is invisible at b3 = 0 by
--   construction. "Religious convergence states" then reads directly: the
--   convergence bit b0 already exists, and b3 is what makes convergence
--   path-dependent rather than a fixed property of the tenet set.

-- The bit is deliberately left UNNAMED. This corpus has eight words already
-- carrying conflicting senses across repositories (VOCABULARY_BOUNDARY.md),
-- and the lesson recorded there is to run the collision check on every
-- coinage or on none. Describing the bit costs nothing; coining for it
-- spends a word before the bit has been tested.


-- ── V. THE CAVEAT THE SOURCE ITSELF RAISES ──────────────────────────────────

-- d-encoding-is-lossy : verify.py:209 states the verdicts "must not be
--   inferred from a lossy B/J/C bit pattern." The bits are a PROJECTION of
--   the verdicts, not a definition of them. Two consequences, both real:
--
--   (1) The grid reading in section II is a reading, not a specification.
--       Four of its eight rows are unattested (d-bits-are-BJC).
--   (2) Extending the ENCODING from 3 bits to 4 does not automatically
--       extend the VERDICTS. If 8 verdicts already exceed what 3 bits
--       capture, then 16 states is a claim about the verdict space that the
--       bit arithmetic cannot establish on its own.
--
--   This does not block the tower. It says the tower must be built on the
--   verdicts and checked against the encoding, not read off the encoding.
--   Doing it the other way round is how a count becomes a fact without
--   being measured -- see counts-in-names-must-be-measured.


-- ── VI. NON-DERIVES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- nd-b3-is-order : that the fourth bit IS measurement-order dependence.
--   Three arguments support it (purpose, asymmetry, doctrine formation).
--   None is a derivation. Tyler said "quantum"; order-effects are the
--   best-evidenced quantum signature in cognition, but not the only one.
--   Complementarity and interference are unexcluded alternatives.

-- nd-16-is-exactly-2x8 : that the quantum layer doubles rather than
--   restructures. Z2^4 is the natural reading of "8 -> 16" and it is the
--   reading taken here, but a 16-state space need not be a product.

-- nd-classical-slice-is-faithful : that the b3 = 0 slice of the 16 is
--   identical to the standalone 8. Under a product it is. Under any
--   non-product 16 it need not be, and the current 8 would then be an
--   approximation rather than a restriction.

-- nd-possibility-is-b4 : the 32-state layer is declared and out of scope.
--   Nothing here constrains it. Do not assume it is modal; it was not said.

-- nd-tower-terminates : "and more later" is open by construction.


