-- ── XVI. THE REDIRECT IN XI WAS WRONG, AND THE GAP IS ONE FUNCTION ──────────
--
-- Section XI concluded "the machinery for doctrine formation is proof_evo.py."
-- I wrote that from a grep of function NAMES. I never read what the module
-- returns. Third instance in one session of publishing a claim that one
-- command would refute -- after the MetaParadox scope error and the
-- preservation all-clear. The peer session made the same redirect from the
-- same inference and caught it by reading.

-- c-proof-evo-does-not-do-it : measured 2026-09-21.
--   proof_evo.py is 1,155 lines of real evolutionary proof search -- MutationOp,
--   a UCB MutationBandit, _mutate, _crossover, _tournament_select, evolve. It
--   is genuinely built, not an enum. But its output type is
--     ProofStatus = {PROVED, REFUTED, UNRESOLVED, EVOLVING}
--   It never assigns a Verdict. It imports Verdict (:58) and READS exactly two,
--   VERIFIED (:681) and CONTRADICTION (:685) -- both from the statically
--   reachable four. Occurrences of the four EXCLUDED verdicts: ZERO.

-- d-the-paradox-half-has-no-producer : the general result, and it is worse
--   than the redirect being wrong.
--   Every appearance of SHADOW_PARADOX or MIRROR_PARADOX in src/ is a
--   COMPARISON, never an assignment:
--     cycle_detector.py:216,217,232,235,252,253,256   trace[i] == ...
--     verify.py:347,351                                self.verdict == ...
--   verify.py refuses to emit them by the enforced invariant (section X).
--   ppl.py names them only in comments and one docstring. training/salience.py
--   assigns them weights. Every one a consumer.
--   And the traces have no producer either: tests/test_cycle_detector.py
--   builds every trace as a hand-written literal -- [V, C, B, X, V, V] and
--   friends. CycleDetector.classify takes a Sequence[Verdict] that NOTHING in
--   the package ever constructs.
--   So the paradox half of the lattice is entirely consumer-side. Four
--   consumers, zero producers, and a test suite that supplies by hand what no
--   code can generate.

-- WHAT SURVIVES, and it is the load-bearing half. ADR 0002's monotonicity
-- argument is a MATHEMATICAL observation, not an implementation claim:
-- monotonicity constrains one formula against its own conjuncts and says
-- nothing about two formulas separated by a mutation. That is true whether or
-- not anyone coded it. So the generational reading remains the only logically
-- available route to paradox-holding, and every consequence drawn from it in
-- sections X and XI stands -- including d-paradox-holding-is-not-conjunction,
-- which is the one that matters for the religion work. Only "the machinery
-- exists" fails. XI needs this paragraph, not a rebuild.

-- d-the-gap-is-one-map : and this is worth more than the redirect was.
--   ProofNode already carries `generation: int` (proof_evo.py:84) and the
--   mutation engine is real. So the generational STRUCTURE exists. What is
--   missing is a single map
--       ProofNode at generation N  ->  Verdict
--   Nothing in the package has it. That map is exactly what would produce the
--   trace CycleDetector.classify was built to consume and never receives. One
--   missing function between two working halves, and it is the function that
--   would make 010 and 011 reachable in fact rather than in principle.
--   This is the most concrete open item in this file.

-- This also corrects section XV's reason for keeping the repository, in the
-- direction of keeping it. proof_evo.py is NOT load-bearing because it
-- implements the semantics -- it does not. It is load-bearing because it is
-- the only place the generational structure exists at all, and it is one
-- function from closing the gap the whole paradox lattice depends on.

-- d-four-instances-of-one-pattern : recorded because the pattern is the find.
--   (1) a constraint that cannot fail       -- ax-p0-no-return, TestMetaParadox
--   (2) a constraint that cannot be satisfied -- the joint-SAT gate, section XI
--   (3) a repair that reduces to what it replaced -- orthomodular/paraconsistent
--   (4) a mechanism named where it is needed and absent where it would run
--                                            -- proof-evolution semantics
--   All four are the same failure: a claim checked against its own statement
--   rather than against something that could refute it. Three of the four were
--   mine or half mine.

-- d-my-own-recurring-error : distinct from the four above, which are the
--   corpus's. Mine is one error repeated: STATING A UNIVERSAL FROM A BOUNDED
--   SEARCH WITHOUT NAMING THE BOUND.
--     "nothing imports MetaParadox, package-wide"   -- searched src/ only
--     "preservation is genuinely complete"          -- counted nothing
--     "hypermath has 23 interior declarations"      -- swept references/ in
--     "719585b exists in none of them"              -- searched 5 of 6 repos
--   Four times in one session, and every one was refutable by a single command.
--   The remediation is not "search harder", it is to WRITE THE BOUND INTO THE
--   SENTENCE: say which paths were searched, and the claim stops being false.
--   The peer's parallel finding is the mirror of this one -- its census number
--   was right while the METHOD SENTENCE it published was unreproducible. Both
--   failures live in the reporting sentence, not in the work.

-- GC-PLT-9  Write the ProofNode -> Verdict map, or record that the generational
--           route is unimplemented wherever sections X-XI are relied on.
--           Until it exists, "paradox-holding is reachable under
--           proof-evolution semantics" is a mathematical claim with no witness.

-- d-the-rule-has-two-limbs : the peer session sharpened the rule above and the
--   sharpening is right. Recorded because the first limb alone looked total.
--
--   LIMB 1 -- UNSTATED BOUND. The claim is unfalsifiable: a reader cannot
--     reproduce it and so cannot refute it. Remedy: disclosure. Name the paths
--     searched in the sentence that reports the search.
--
--   LIMB 2 -- WRONG BOUND. The claim is falsifiable, reproducible, AND FALSE.
--     Disclosure does not touch it, because a well-stated bound can be the
--     wrong bound. Remedy: justify the CHOICE of bound against the adjacent
--     one that was not taken.
--
--   All four of my instances are limb 1. The peer's census was limb 2 wearing
--   limb 1's clothes: its number 17 was correct, its published method
--   ("over each repo's *.hm") was unreproducible, and what made 17 right was
--   never the glob -- it was the unargued judgement that references/precursor
--   holds vendored []-system material rather than hypermath's layer stack.
--   Swap that judgement and the same well-bounded sentence reports 23 and is
--   reproducibly false. I accepted the limb-1 framing when it was offered and
--   that acceptance was itself the error.

-- d-limb-2-applied-to-the-bound-that-found-it : immediately, and it holds.
--   The peer's durability measurement was bounded to TOP-LEVEL *.hm ACROSS
--   FIVE REPOS. Both halves of that bound are choices, neither argued, and
--   widening either changes the result:
--
--   the repo bound. The five were hyperlogic, metamathethicology, hyperethics,
--     hypermath, hyperphysics. It omitted meta-morphoscripted-origination --
--     ITS OWN REPO, and the one holding PLACEMENT.md and SCOPE.md, where
--     today's placement decisions live. Measured: that repo is 9 AHEAD of its
--     remote, so the report's clause "all five repos are 0 ahead of their
--     remotes" is true of the five measured and false of the sixth. That is
--     the 719585b error, made by the session correcting the 719585b error, in
--     the message correcting it.
--     It also omitted formal-universality, which is strictly worse than
--     anything in the list: 6 top-level *.hm, ZERO tracked, ONE commit, and
--     NO REMOTE CONFIGURED AT ALL.
--
--   the filetype bound. *.hm only. Widening to top-level *.md finds the
--     untracked set is 14 files, not 8, and the additions are load-bearing:
--     metamathethicology/VOCABULARY_BOUNDARY.md, hypermath/P0_STATUS.md,
--     hyperphysics/P0_PRECONDITION.md, hyperethics/MIGRATION.md.
--
--   NEITHER WIDENING WEAKENS THE FINDING. Both strengthen it. That is the
--   point of limb 2: the bound was not chosen to flatter the conclusion, it
--   was simply never argued, and an unargued bound is right by luck.

-- GC-PLT-10 Every census in this corpus states its bound. From now it also
--           states WHY THAT BOUND AND NOT THE ADJACENT ONE. A stated bound
--           makes a claim checkable; only a justified bound makes it right.
